    "turn_idx": 57,
    "turn_text": "in the NFL, you have people who are professionals who see things coming. And just like in any other job, you know, if you're waiting on something, you know, you can jump on. And so that's why I, you know, sometimes seem so fast in the NFL because, you know, a guy might know that that's coming and he's all over it, you know, and that's just the way it is. And these are, you know, it's, it's, um, It's a grown man sport. It's definitely in the NFL business. But I really enjoyed my teammates. I was lucky enough to be at the same place for five years before I hurt my neck. There were a lot of guys, unfortunately, bouncing around a bit. So I got to be in one place with one coaching staff for most of the time. People ask me, what do you miss about the NFL? I always tell them, you know, it's the locker room, you know, because you walk into our locker room and it was like a comedy club, first of all. I mean, it's so, so funny. I mean, there's always something outrageous happening. And you got the country's voice from the furthest out and the kids from the middle of the city who really had never left it, who are friends and who are working together and getting along. You've got people of all different backgrounds from all over the country. And we've got to come together as one team. And I always say, I wish more people in Congress had to play team sports, because I feel like if you did, And you learn something about where you fit into things and how your role is sometimes to help others.",
