    "turn_idx": 95,
    "turn_text": "was here at this school with all these people who had fancy cars and fancy clothes. And I felt completely like a fish out of water. And I wanted to go home. And, you know, and I eventually just realized that the harder I worked, the luckier I got. But, you know, I had a lot of help along the way. And, you know, when you, when you treat people well, in my experience, as you're going through life, They'll be there for you too when you need them. And it's in the strangest ways. It's people who you never thought you were going to have another conversation with maybe. But to those kids, I always tell them when I go to schools, particularly in Dallas, I say, I've been sitting in your exact seat. I promise you that whatever your home life situation is, it's not that different than mine was. And I'm here to tell you that the range of options is much broader than you can even imagine. When I was in school, I mean, we thought if you were smart, they said you should be a doctor or a lawyer. And so when I went to Baylor, I first tried to be a doctor.",
